You know, it reminds me very much of watching my first graders Zoom classes.

785
00:32:24.940 --> 00:32:27.040
Oh, trying to keep people on task.

786
00:32:27.040 --> 00:32:27.760
Yes.

787
00:32:28.080 --> 00:32:31.520
The teacher is like, what is three plus two?

788
00:32:31.780 --> 00:32:33.740
And everyone's like, I got a new puppy.

789
00:32:34.540 --> 00:32:35.940
It's loud outside.

790
00:32:36.480 --> 00:32:37.940
My mom likes wine.

791
00:32:38.340 --> 00:32:41.100
And the teacher is like, what is three plus two?

792
00:32:42.280 --> 00:32:45.460
That is this is what it reminds me of.

793
00:32:45.960 --> 00:32:50.700
Daryl trying to talk to all of us about this forklift and this bailer.

794
00:32:50.700 --> 00:33:00.120
You know, Harold Ramis talked about Craig and about how brilliant of an actor he thought he was and how he felt like Craig was a naturalistic actor.

795
00:33:00.300 --> 00:33:08.120
Like it was so natural, this dialogue coming out of him that you just wholeheartedly believe him.

796
00:33:08.540 --> 00:33:10.940
It never seems scripted, right?

797
00:33:11.180 --> 00:33:16.020
Like everything about his cadence, like all of it.

798
00:33:16.120 --> 00:33:17.280
It's so it is.

799
00:33:17.420 --> 00:33:18.060
It's amazing.

800
00:33:18.400 --> 00:33:18.800
Yeah.

801
00:33:19.380 --> 00:33:21.040
I was sort of studying that.

802
00:33:21.180 --> 00:33:23.620
That's so funny that Harold Ramis said that because I was studying that.

803
00:33:23.680 --> 00:33:25.800
I was like, how does he make it seem so natural?

804
00:33:26.500 --> 00:33:28.920
He's I mean, Craig is really brilliant, guys.

805
00:33:29.140 --> 00:33:30.060
He's super talented.

806
00:33:30.280 --> 00:33:31.780
Craig, come be on the podcaSt.

807
00:33:32.220 --> 00:33:33.320
I reached out to him.

808
00:33:33.480 --> 00:33:34.440
We've traded some messages.

809
00:33:34.440 --> 00:33:35.320
It's going to happen.

810
00:33:35.440 --> 00:33:36.980
We just have to figure out dates.

811
00:33:37.160 --> 00:33:38.180
Let's lock it up, Craig.

812
00:33:38.340 --> 00:33:39.020
Let's lock it up.

813
00:33:39.020 --> 00:33:43.780
Well, as Daryl is explaining the dangers of the bailer.

