00:59:16.800 --> 00:59:17.300
What did he say?

1388
00:59:17.520 --> 00:59:18.460
This is what he said.

1389
00:59:18.840 --> 00:59:23.360
He wrote, I definitely bit right into that potato, and it wasn't half bad.

1390
00:59:24.260 --> 00:59:24.740
Oh.

1391
00:59:25.720 --> 00:59:26.840
So there you go.

1392
00:59:27.060 --> 00:59:28.100
There you go.

1393
00:59:28.600 --> 00:59:35.340
Well, Angela, it makes sense to me because in French, the word for apple is pom, and the

1394
00:59:35.340 --> 00:59:41.160
word for potato is pom de terre, which means apple of the earth or apple of the ground.

1395
00:59:41.160 --> 00:59:42.160
I'm sorry.

1396
00:59:42.260 --> 00:59:42.980
What is your logic?

1397
00:59:43.420 --> 00:59:48.820
It makes sense to you that Creed would eat a potato and not know it wasn't an apple because

1398
00:59:48.820 --> 00:59:50.740
it's the French word is pom de terre?

1399
00:59:51.660 --> 00:59:51.780
Yeah.

1400
00:59:52.080 --> 00:59:52.260
Okay.

1401
00:59:53.520 --> 00:59:56.060
Potato in Indonesian is kintang.

1402
00:59:56.420 --> 00:59:57.540
What's apple?

1403
00:59:57.740 --> 00:59:58.820
Apple is appel.

1404
00:59:59.380 --> 00:59:59.600
Oh.

1405
00:59:59.860 --> 01:00:05.280
Well, the French have related the apple and the potato in their language.

1406
01:00:05.520 --> 01:00:05.780
Okay.

1407
01:00:05.780 --> 01:00:11.920
And so perhaps, perhaps they, I don't know, they're onto something.

1408
01:00:12.180 --> 01:00:14.020
Perhaps Creed would do well in France.

1409
01:00:14.620 --> 01:00:15.220
Yeah.

1410
01:00:15.500 --> 01:00:16.780
I guess that's right.

1411
01:00:16.780 --> 01:00:19.920
But as long as he doesn't try to pick them up himself at a market.

1412
01:00:20.280 --> 01:00:21.400
And thump them.

1413
01:00:21.780 --> 01:00:29.560
Before we leave the whole Creed betting scene, at 12 minutes, 38 seconds, you can see Angela

1414
01:00:29.560 --> 01:00:32.860
