1719
01:16:02.600 --> 01:16:04.380
That's very parent mode, right?

1720
01:16:04.980 --> 01:16:05.360
Yeah.

1721
01:16:05.680 --> 01:16:05.900
Come inside.

1722
01:16:05.940 --> 01:16:07.920
I've got a treat for you.

1723
01:16:08.320 --> 01:16:10.020
Stop doing what you're doing.

1724
01:16:11.240 --> 01:16:23.740
I love hearing what BJ's thought process was when he was writing these scenes, because something I really appreciated about them was that Pam and Jim were not laughing about this.

1725
01:16:23.960 --> 01:16:24.040
No.

1726
01:16:24.720 --> 01:16:26.560
This was not a joke to them.

1727
01:16:26.900 --> 01:16:32.780
When they realized what Michael was doing, they come together very seriously to help him.

1728
01:16:33.000 --> 01:16:34.680
This also was not flirty.

1729
01:16:35.000 --> 01:16:39.520
This was not a flirty moment, but instead really highlighted their bond.

1730
01:16:40.020 --> 01:16:40.300
Yeah.

1731
01:16:40.520 --> 01:16:46.480
And just the fact that instantly the two of them knew what Michael was up to.

1732
01:16:46.880 --> 01:16:50.060
And it's like everything else didn't matter.

1733
01:16:50.320 --> 01:16:58.200
It didn't matter that they had hurt feelings over Roy, over Karen, over everything that has happened between the two of them.

1734
01:16:58.360 --> 01:16:59.240
None of that mattered.

1735
01:16:59.480 --> 01:17:03.160
All that mattered was getting Michael off the roof safely.

1736
01:17:03.740 --> 01:17:04.980
And that's what happens.

1737
01:17:05.260 --> 01:17:07.240
